{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Avram journeyed, going on and journeying toward the Negev.</b> The purpose of all his journeys, every one — that he would travel and pitch camp now here, now there — was nothing other than the portion of Judah, which is in the south of the land of Israel, and that is Mount Moriah; this is its plain sense. And included in it as well: 'going on and journeying toward the Negev' — rung after rung, journey after journey, the movement of the rational soul and the stilling of the body. From this it first says 'ויט אהלה' (he inclined his tent), and it further says shortly after, 'ויאהל אברם ויבא וישב' (Avram pitched his tent and came and dwelt). And all these journeys were in order to attain the attainment of the prophecy of El Shaddai, which is the appellation of Alef-Dalet that he attained, which is embraced by the term הנגבה (toward the Negev); therefore he mentions it constantly in his words: 'אדני ה' מה תתן לי' (Adonai YHWH, what will You give me), 'אדני ה' במה אדע' (Adonai YHWH, whereby shall I know)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The phrase 'כנוי של אל״ף דל״ת' refers to the divine name Adonai (אדני) by which Avram addresses YHWH; rendered as 'the appellation of Alef-Dalet' preserving the author's letter-based reference."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:00.751295085Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}